window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-63860b400c19c9e9"]={"key":"ny_main-63860b400c19c9e9","group":"ny_main","uid":"63860b400c19c9e9","rank":31,"title":"gdpval authored doc wexmoor returns 001","occupation":"general_operations_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are the enterprise retail operations manager at Vellumstone Associates, advising Nadia Sepulveda on the control Wexmoor Press will pilot at its only retail site and then use as the enterprise baseline. The seasonal promotion starts 15 September 2025, so Nadia needs a decision this week between the current cashier-led process and a proposed portal-only process with central approval. The current process is quick, but staff use “sale date” to mean either payment or collection and there is no common exception log. The portal is being phased in from 15 September through 31 October while till slips remain valid; its sole central reviewer can clear 35 requests a day against a forecast peak of 60, and there is no budget for temporary cover. The governing house policy says, “Unopened goods may be returned within 30 days of sale date; hygiene-sealed personal-care goods are excluded once the seal is broken; clearance goods are excluded from change-of-mind returns.” The procedure must be suitable for England and Wales as at 8 September 2025 and must not silently widen or contract customers’ legal rights. No attachments are coming. The recoverable comparison summary for 1 March–31 May 2024 is 1,240 lines and £74,880, including 28 exact duplicate lines worth £1,680 and 14 malformed-ID lines worth £910; nine malformed lines worth £590 can be linked unambiguously, leaving five worth £320 unresolved. For 1 March–31 May 2025 it is 1,390 lines and £91,540, including 71 exact duplicates worth £4,870 and 23 malformed-ID lines worth £1,740; 15 worth £1,060 can be linked, leaving eight worth £680 unresolved. These groups do not overlap, and no line-level re-export will be available before sign-off. Create `wexmoor_returns_decision_and_procedure.xlsx` as one editable workbook with clearly labelled Decision, Operating Procedure, Comparison, and Change Log sections. Give Nadia one justified recommendation, an approval-ready procedure that works during the transition and in the end state, matching period figures with a material-change explanation, and a record of judgments and changes. Keep Decision to one printed page and Operating Procedure to no more than two printed pages; supporting sections may extend beyond that. Do not invent missing figures or present the workbook as legal advice. Write the file at the top level of the working directory using exactly that filename.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `wexmoor_returns_decision_and_procedure.xlsx` — Editable decision workbook containing the recommendation, returns operating procedure, comparison analysis, and change record. (Place the file at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename.; Include clearly labelled Decision, Operating Procedure, Comparison, and Change Log sections.; Keep the Decision section to one printed page and the Operating Procedure section to no more than two printed pages.; Keep formulas, assumptions, and change records editable and inspectable.; Do not use macros, external data connections, or links that are required to read or recalculate the workbook.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/wexmoor_returns_decision_and_procedure.xlsx","bytes":25939,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/55a6993213a6ad6f633fb8792110f2ba4990f2e240f6545e572863d3d3e17787.xlsx","sha256":"55a6993213a6ad6f633fb8792110f2ba4990f2e240f6545e572863d3d3e17787","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Decision","row_count":25,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Wexmoor Press - Returns Control Decision","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["For Nadia Sepulveda | Retail-site pilot and future enterprise baseline | England and Wales | Legal and policy position as at 8 September 2025","","",""]},{"r":"3","cells":["Decision","Operating Procedure","Comparison","Change Log"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Recommendation","","",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["Approve adoption of the portal-based returns control as the pilot and enterprise baseline, using bounded site-manager delegation for defined routine voluntary-policy cases and central triage for exceptions. Do not implement immediate portal-only central approval: the stronger portal framework is retained, but central-only approval cannot clear forecast peak demand without weakening service or control.","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["","","",""]},{"r":"8","cells":["This is an operational control recommendation, not legal advice. Staff must keep voluntary change-of-mind, distance-cancellation, and statutory-remedy assessments separate and escalate uncertainty.","","",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["Decision Comparison","","",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["Criterion","Current cashier-led process","Proposed portal-only central approval","Approved controlled portal model"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Control consistency","Quick, but staff use 'sale date' as payment or collection and there is no common exception log.","One ruleset and central queue; consistent review logic, but every case waits for the sole reviewer.","Portal rules, one case record and mandatory exception capture; local authority is limited to routine, verified voluntary-policy cases."]},{"r":"13","cells":["Customer handling","Immediate interaction, but outcomes can vary between cashiers and rights may be described inconsistently.","Predictable handling, but a peak queue can delay an answer or refund for routine customers.","Routine eligible cases can be resolved at site; exceptions receive a recorded hold, clear explanation and central review."]},{"r":"14","cells":["Auditability","Till evidence is available, but exceptions are not held in a common log and duplicate checks are weak.","Portal record supports traceability, approval evidence and exception reporting.","One Return Case ID or cross-reference, daily dual-system reconciliation and a defined audit record."]},{"r":"15","cells":["Capacity","Site capacity is available, but with unrestricted process variation rather than a controlled decision boundary.","35 central requests/day against a forecast 60/day peak leaves an unworkable 25 requests/day shortfall; no temporary-cover budget.","Central capacity is reserved for legally sensitive, disputed, ambiguous or exceptional cases; no unrestricted cashier discretion."]},{"r":"16","cells":["Transition feasibility","Familiar today, but it would preserve the ambiguous date and missing-log weaknesses.","Portal phases in 15 September-31 October while valid till slips remain evidence; central-only routing is infeasible at peak.","Transition accepts till-slip and portal evidence, assigns one case ID and reconciles daily; portal is authoritative after 31 October."]},{"r":"18","cells":["Formula-linked Evidence","","",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["Measure","Prior / capacity","Current / peak","Decision implication"]},{"r":"20","cells":["Central review flow","=Comparison!B40  [缓存: 35]","=Comparison!B41  [缓存: 60]","=C20-B20  [缓存: 25]"]},{"r":"21","cells":["Confirmed lines","=Comparison!B27  [缓存: 1207]","=Comparison!C27  [缓存: 1311]","=Comparison!D27  [缓存: 104]"]},{"r":"22","cells":["Confirmed value","=Comparison!B28  [缓存: 72880]","=Comparison!C28  [缓存: 85990]","=Comparison!D28  [缓存: 13110]"]},{"r":"23","cells":["Exact-duplicate line rate","=Comparison!B31  [缓存: 0.0225806451612903]","=Comparison!C31  [缓存: 0.0510791366906475]","=Comparison!D31  [缓存: 2.84984915293572]"]},{"r":"24","cells":["Raw vs confirmed value movement","=Comparison!D29  [缓存: 16660]","=Comparison!D28  [缓存: 13110]","=Comparison!D32  [缓存: 3550]"]},{"r":"25","cells":["=\"Comparison reading: confirmed activity grew (lines +\"&TEXT(Comparison!D27,\"#,##0\")&\" / \"&TEXT(Comparison!E27,\"0.0%\")&\"; value +£\"&TEXT(Comparison!D28,\"#,##0\")&\" / \"&TEXT(Comparison!E28,\"0.0%\")&\") while duplicate incidence worsened from \"&TEXT(Comparison!B31,\"0.0%\")&\" to \"&TEXT(Comparison!C31,\"0.0%\")&\" (+\"&TEXT(Comparison!D31,\"0.00\")&\" pp). Raw value rose £\"&TEXT(Comparison!D29,\"#,##0\")&\"; confirmed value rose £\"&TEXT(Comparison!D28,\"#,##0\")&\". The £\"&TEXT(Comparison!D32,\"#,##0\")&\" difference is the increased adjustment burden, not a substitute for confirmed growth.\"  [缓存: Comparison reading: confirmed activity grew (lines +104 / 8.6%; value +£13,110 / 18.0%) while duplicate incidence worsened from 2.3% to 5.1% (+2.85 pp). Raw value rose £16,660; confirmed value rose £13,110. The £3,550 difference is the increased adjustment burden, not a substitute for confirmed growth.]","","",""]},{"r":"26","cells":["Approval Call","","",""]},{"r":"27","cells":["Approval sought this week: approve the controlled portal and triage model for the 15 September-31 October transition and its portal-authoritative end state from 1 November 2025. This replaces the unchanged cashier-led process and avoids infeasible immediate portal-only central approval; implementation remains subject to Nadia Sepulveda's approval of this draft.","","",""]},{"r":"28","cells":["","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Operating Procedure","row_count":29,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Wexmoor Press - Returns Operating Procedure","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Approval-ready draft | England and Wales | Legal and policy position as at 8 September 2025 | Applies to retail-site pilot and enterprise baseline","","",""]},{"r":"3","cells":["Decision","Operating Procedure","Comparison","Change Log"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Document owner","Enterprise Retail Operations Manager, Vellumstone Associates","Approver","Nadia Sepulveda"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Version / status","0.9 | Draft - pending approval","Intended dates","Transition 15 September 2025 to 31 October 2025; end state 1 November 2025"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Purpose, scope and audience: control customer returns at Wexmoor Press's retail site during the pilot and as the future enterprise baseline. Used by frontline staff, site managers/delegated approvers, central review and compliance reviewers. It is operational guidance, not legal advice or a complete statement of consumer rights.","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["Non-negotiable boundary: classify the customer's route before applying the house policy. The 30-day house rule is voluntary change-of-mind policy; statutory remedies and qualifying distance-sale cancellation rights are assessed separately and must not be narrowed by clearance, opening, a broken hygiene seal or expiry of the house-policy window.","","",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["A. Classify the Route Before Any Eligibility Decision","","",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["Route / check","Staff action","Control and legal qualification","Record / escalation"]},{"r":"11","cells":["1. Voluntary change of mind","Use only where the customer seeks a discretionary return of satisfactory goods. Apply the house rule: verify timely return, credible purchase evidence, unopened goods, relevant product status and delegated authority.","An in-store customer does not generally have a statutory right to return satisfactory goods merely for changing their mind. Apply any available house-policy entitlement, but do not describe it as the full measure of statutory rights.","Record route as 'voluntary'. If the customer mentions a fault, description, fitness or quality issue, stop this route and use route 3."]},{"r":"12","cells":["2. Distance cancellation / click-and-collect","For a qualifying distance contract, use the separate usual 14-day cancellation period measured from receipt of goods; do not apply it automatically to ordinary in-store sales. For click-and-collect, establish where and how the contract was concluded.","Collection itself does not classify the contract. Distinguish an online purchase completed online from an online reservation completed in store. Escalate unclear channel or cancellation eligibility to central review.","Record channel, contract-conclusion evidence and receipt/collection date. Keep cancellation route separate from voluntary and quality routes."]},{"r":"13","cells":["3. Quality / defect claim","If goods are alleged faulty, not as described, unfit for purpose or of unsatisfactory quality, route to statutory-remedy assessment. Capture the allegation and any disclosed defect information without promising a remedy.","Do not reject solely because goods are clearance, opened, hygiene-related, seal-broken or outside the voluntary 30-day window. Any Consumer Rights Act short-term right to reject concerns nonconforming goods, has its own conditions/timing and is not an unopened-goods rule or the house policy.","Central review decides disputed, legally sensitive or exceptional statutory cases. Keep goods segregated where appropriate pending assessment."]},{"r":"14","cells":["4. Date, evidence and product checks","House-policy eligibility date only: immediate in-store supply = date customer takes possession; advance-paid click-and-collect = collection date; delivered order = delivery date. Treat that event as day 0 and count day 1 from the following day through day 30.","This day count is an internal voluntary-policy eligibility rule, not a clock for every statutory remedy. Ask for receipt, order record, payment record or till/order lookup; an original paper receipt is not the only credible evidence.","If purchase evidence or transaction identity cannot be verified, record what was presented and escalate; do not promise approval. Record date basis and date used."]},{"r":"15","cells":["5. Clearance and hygiene rules","For voluntary change-of-mind only, clearance goods are excluded. A relevant hygiene-sealed personal-care good is excluded only where a suitable hygiene/health-protection seal existed and has been broken.","Do not treat every personal-care item, opened package or hygiene label as an automatic bar. A defect disclosed before sale differs from a different or undisclosed defect; statutory assessment remains available where raised.","Record clearance status, seal presence/broken state and any disclosed-defect wording. Escalate disputed condition or disclosure."]},{"r":"17","cells":["B. Execute, Record and Reconcile the Return","","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["Step / owner","Action","Authority / triage","Record, customer and closure"]},{"r":"19","cells":["1. Intake\nFrontline staff","Acknowledge the request, inspect the item only as needed for route/condition, collect proportionate evidence and create one Return Case ID before any refund or refusal. Do not collect unnecessary sensitive personal data.","Frontline staff may intake, inspect and record. They do not waive policy conditions, decide statutory disputes or finalise an exception.","Capture original transaction reference, channel, date basis/date, route/reason, item, condition/seal where relevant, evidence source and intake timestamp."]},{"r":"20","cells":["2. Routine decision\nSite manager / delegated approver","For a fully verified routine voluntary-policy case, test timeliness, credible proof, unopened condition, clearance/hygiene restriction and prior-refund search. Approve or refuse with a clear reason.","May approve only a routine case that meets every documented house-policy test. Cannot waive time, condition or product exclusions; cannot determine a statutory, disputed, ambiguous or duplicate-risk case.","Record decision, authority, value, refund/refusal outcome and timestamp. Explain the route and reason without suggesting policy removes statutory rights."]},{"r":"21","cells":["3. Central triage\nCentral reviewer","Queue legally sensitive, disputed, ambiguous or exceptional cases: unclear contract channel, disputed condition/disclosed defect, unresolved transaction identity, suspected duplicate refund, statutory-rights challenge or outside delegated authority.","Central reviewer has final exception authority. Capacity is 35 requests/day against forecast peak 60; no temporary cover is assumed. Routine cases stay within the bounded local authority rather than recreating unrestricted cashier discretion.","Record hold/escalation reason, queue status, reviewer decision and customer update. Do not make a final statutory refusal at site while review is pending."]},{"r":"22","cells":["4. Refund, stock and closure\nApprover / frontline","Process approved refund through the controlled route, mark the case outcome, and prevent a second refund. Return only appropriate sellable goods to stock; segregate alleged faulty or uncertain goods pending the relevant assessment.","No unlogged refund. A refusal must be evidence-based, use the correct route and identify escalation where applicable.","Close only after outcome, value, authority and timestamps are recorded and the case is reconciled. Retain no unnecessary sensitive personal data."]},{"r":"24","cells":["C. Migration, End State and Continuity","","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["Period / owner","Required operating model","Anti-duplication and authority control","Record / completion"]},{"r":"26","cells":["15 Sep-31 Oct 2025\nSite manager","Accept both valid till-slip and portal evidence while the portal is phased in. Allocate a portal Return Case ID where available; otherwise allocate a controlled transition-log ID and enter/cross-reference it when portal access is available.","Search the portal, transition log and till/refund record before payment. The site manager reconciles Return Case IDs, till slips, refunds, pending central queue and portal entries each day; investigate and hold suspected duplicate payment.","One return must have one case identifier or a documented cross-reference. Capture both evidence references where present and mark the final outcome in the authoritative case record."]},{"r":"27","cells":["From 1 Nov 2025\nSite manager / central review","The portal is the authoritative returns register. Routine approvals remain limited to the defined delegated path and are entered in the portal; exception classes remain in the central-review queue.","Do not revert to a silent till-only process. Continue duplicate search before refund and close cases only after portal record and outcome are complete.","Use the portal record for audit reporting, exception review and reconciliation; retain supporting evidence reference rather than unnecessary personal data."]},{"r":"28","cells":["Portal outage\nSite manager","Use the controlled outage queue with a pre-assigned Return Case ID, full minimum record and evidence reference. Apply the same route and authority limits; no unlogged refund or exception waiver.","On restoration, enter every queued record into the portal, cross-reference the outage ID and reconcile any refund before closure. Escalate duplicate-risk or missing-identity cases.","Record outage start/end, portal capture timestamp and reconciler. Keep the queue available for audit until reconciliation is complete."]},{"r":"30","cells":["Minimum return record: Return Case ID; original transaction reference; channel and contract/date basis; route/reason; item and relevant seal/condition; purchase evidence reference; decision and authority; value; refund/refusal/hold outcome; intake, decision and closure timestamps; transition/outage cross-reference where used. Keep data proportionate and do not solicit unnecessary sensitive personal data.","","",""]},{"r":"31","cells":["","","",""]},{"r":"32","cells":["Escalation destination and holding action: central review for unclear channel, disputed condition or disclosed defect, unresolved transaction identity, suspected duplicate refund, customer challenge involving statutory rights, or any case outside delegated authority. Record the hold and customer communication; do not leave the case at a dead end or present a policy refusal as a legal conclusion.","","",""]},{"r":"33","cells":["","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Comparison","row_count":41,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Wexmoor Press - Returns Comparison and Data Adjustment","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Recoverable period summaries | 1 Mar-31 May 2024 vs 1 Mar-31 May 2025 | Inputs are shaded yellow; editable formulas are shaded green","","","","",""]},{"r":"3","cells":["Decision","Operating Procedure","Comparison","Change Log"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Method: remove each exact duplicate once. Duplicate and malformed-ID groups are non-overlapping. Unambiguously linked malformed-ID records remain in the confirmed population; unresolved malformed-ID records remain visible but are excluded from confirmed figures without being treated as proven invalid transactions.","","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Scope limitation: no line-level re-export was available before sign-off. These summaries do not support invented transaction-level facts, product, customer, reason, channel or approval conclusions. England and Wales operational context as at 8 September 2025.","","","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["A. Supplied Summary Inputs and Reconciliation","","","","",""]},{"r":"8","cells":["Component","2024 lines","2024 value","2025 lines","2025 value","Treatment / trace"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Raw recoverable comparison population","1240","74880","1390","91540","Starting population in the recoverable comparison summary."]},{"r":"10","cells":["Exact duplicate lines","28","1680","71","4870","Remove once from confirmed population. This group does not overlap with malformed IDs."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Malformed-ID population","14","910","23","1740","Reconciled below; malformed ID alone is not a reason to remove a linked record."]},{"r":"12","cells":["  Linked unambiguously","9","590","15","1060","Retain in confirmed population; original ID was malformed but link is unambiguous."]},{"r":"13","cells":["  Unresolved","5","320","8","680","Separate unresolved population. Exclude from confirmed figures, not proven invalid."]},{"r":"14","cells":["Malformed-ID reconciliation check","=B12+B13  [缓存: 14]","=C12+C13  [缓存: 910]","=D12+D13  [缓存: 23]","=E12+E13  [缓存: 1740]","Linked plus unresolved must equal the malformed-ID population."]},{"r":"16","cells":["B. Formula-derived Confirmed Population","","","","",""]},{"r":"17","cells":["Calculation","2024 lines","2024 value","2025 lines","2025 value","Formula treatment"]},{"r":"18","cells":["Raw population","=B9  [缓存: 1240]","=C9  [缓存: 74880]","=D9  [缓存: 1390]","=E9  [缓存: 91540]","Starting point."]},{"r":"19","cells":["Less exact duplicates","=B10  [缓存: 28]","=C10  [缓存: 1680]","=D10  [缓存: 71]","=E10  [缓存: 4870]","Deduct once only."]},{"r":"20","cells":["Less unresolved malformed IDs","=B13  [缓存: 5]","=C13  [缓存: 320]","=D13  [缓存: 8]","=E13  [缓存: 680]","Exclude from confirmed; keep visible as uncertainty."]},{"r":"21","cells":["Confirmed population","=B18-B19-B20  [缓存: 1207]","=C18-C19-C20  [缓存: 72880]","=D18-D19-D20  [缓存: 1311]","=E18-E19-E20  [缓存: 85990]","Raw less exact duplicates less unresolved malformed IDs."]},{"r":"22","cells":["Linked malformed IDs retained","=B12  [缓存: 9]","=C12  [缓存: 590]","=D12  [缓存: 15]","=E12  [缓存: 1060]","Included within confirmed population; not a deduction."]},{"r":"23","cells":["Total exclusions","=B19+B20  [缓存: 33]","=C19+C20  [缓存: 2000]","=D19+D20  [缓存: 79]","=E19+E20  [缓存: 5550]","Duplicate plus unresolved-ID exclusion burden."]},{"r":"25","cells":["C. Period Movement and Data-quality Signal","","","","",""]},{"r":"26","cells":["Metric","2024","2025","Movement","% / pp","Interpretation"]},{"r":"27","cells":["Confirmed line count","=B21  [缓存: 1207]","=D21  [缓存: 1311]","=C27-B27  [缓存: 104]","=D27/B27  [缓存: 0.0861640430820215]","Confirmed growth; percentage uses 2024 confirmed count."]},{"r":"28","cells":["Confirmed value","=C21  [缓存: 72880]","=E21  [缓存: 85990]","=C28-B28  [缓存: 13110]","=D28/B28  [缓存: 0.179884742041712]","Confirmed growth; percentage uses 2024 confirmed value."]},{"r":"29","cells":["Raw value","=C9  [缓存: 74880]","=E9  [缓存: 91540]","=C29-B29  [缓存: 16660]","=D29/B29  [缓存: 0.222489316239316]","Unadjusted movement before exclusions."]},{"r":"30","cells":["Total exclusion burden","=C23  [缓存: 2000]","=E23  [缓存: 5550]","=C30-B30  [缓存: 3550]","","Increase in duplicate plus unresolved-ID adjustments."]},{"r":"31","cells":["Exact-duplicate line rate","=B10/B9  [缓存: 0.0225806451612903]","=D10/D9  [缓存: 0.0510791366906475]","=(C31-B31)*100  [缓存: 2.84984915293572]","","Deterioration expressed as percentage points."]},{"r":"32","cells":["Raw less confirmed value movement","","","=D29-D28  [缓存: 3550]","","Difference caused by higher period-on-period adjustment burden."]},{"r":"34","cells":["=\"Material change explanation: confirmed lines increased from \"&TEXT(B21,\"#,##0\")&\" to \"&TEXT(D21,\"#,##0\")&\" (+\"&TEXT(D27,\"#,##0\")&\"; \"&TEXT(E27,\"0.0%\")&\"). Confirmed value increased from £\"&TEXT(C21,\"#,##0\")&\" to £\"&TEXT(E21,\"#,##0\")&\" (+£\"&TEXT(D28,\"#,##0\")&\"; \"&TEXT(E28,\"0.0%\")&\"). This is genuine confirmed growth, alongside weaker data quality: exact-duplicate incidence rose from about \"&TEXT(B31,\"0.0%\")&\" to \"&TEXT(C31,\"0.0%\")&\" (+\"&TEXT(D31,\"0.00\")&\" pp). Raw value rose £\"&TEXT(D29,\"#,##0\")&\"; confirmed value rose £\"&TEXT(D28,\"#,##0\")&\". The £\"&TEXT(D32,\"#,##0\")&\" difference is the larger period-on-period adjustment burden (£\"&TEXT(B30,\"#,##0\")&\" in 2024 to £\"&TEXT(C30,\"#,##0\")&\" in 2025), not an assertion that unresolved lines are invalid.\"  [缓存: Material change explanation: confirmed lines increased from 1,207 to 1,311 (+104; 8.6%). Confirmed value increased from £72,880 to £85,990 (+£13,110; 18.0%). This is genuine confirmed growth, alongside weaker data quality: exact-duplicate incidence rose from about 2.3% to 5.1% (+2.85 pp). Raw value rose £16,660; confirmed value rose £13,110. The £3,550 difference is the larger period-on-period adjustment burden (£2,000 in 2024 to £5,550 in 2025), not an assertion that unresolved lines are invalid.]","","","","",""]},{"r":"35","cells":["","","","","",""]},{"r":"36","cells":["","","","","",""]},{"r":"38","cells":["D. Operational Capacity Inputs","","","","",""]},{"r":"39","cells":["Control input","Value","Unit","Use in decision","",""]},{"r":"40","cells":["Central reviewer capacity","35","requests/day","Available capacity for central exception review.","",""]},{"r":"41","cells":["Forecast peak demand","60","requests/day","Peak demand forecast for the promotion.","",""]},{"r":"42","cells":["Central-review shortfall","=B41-B40  [缓存: 25]","requests/day","Peak demand less capacity; supports bounded local routine authority.","",""]},{"r":"43","cells":["Temporary-cover budget","0","GBP","No temporary cover is available in the stated scenario.","",""]},{"r":"45","cells":["Assumptions and limits: the comparison uses the recoverable summary only; no line-level re-export is available before sign-off. Exact duplicates and malformed-ID groups are stated to be non-overlapping. Each exact duplicate is removed once. Linked malformed records are retained because the linkage is unambiguous. Unresolved malformed records are excluded from confirmed figures but remain a visible uncertain population; they are not labelled duplicate, fraudulent or invalid. No transaction-level facts beyond the supplied summary have been inferred.","","","","",""]},{"r":"46","cells":["","","","","",""]},{"r":"47","cells":["","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Change Log","row_count":13,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Wexmoor Press - Returns Control Change Log","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Document 0.9 | Draft - pending approval | Owner: Enterprise Retail Operations Manager, Vellumstone Associates | Approver: Nadia Sepulveda","","",""]},{"r":"3","cells":["Decision","Operating Procedure","Comparison","Change Log"]},{"r":"5","cells":["This log records substantive operating, policy-boundary and analytical judgments. Status is pending approval unless an approval trace says otherwise; this draft is not represented as already approved.","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["Date / issue","Change or judgment","Rationale","Status / approval trace"]},{"r":"8","cells":["08 Sep 2025\n0.9 / Decision","Recommend the portal control framework with bounded delegation and central triage; do not implement immediate portal-only central approval.","Central capacity is 35 requests/day against 60/day forecast peak, creating a 25/day shortfall; no temporary cover budget.","Draft | Owner: Enterprise Retail Operations Manager | Pending Nadia Sepulveda approval; no approval recorded."]},{"r":"9","cells":["08 Sep 2025\n0.9 / Procedure A4","Replace ambiguous 'sale date' with house-policy eligibility date: physical supply, collection or delivery; event is day 0 and count starts next day.","Creates a consistent internal voluntary-policy window without asserting a statutory timing rule.","Draft | Owner: Enterprise Retail Operations Manager | Pending Nadia Sepulveda approval."]},{"r":"10","cells":["08 Sep 2025\n0.9 / Procedure A1-A5","Separate voluntary change-of-mind, distance cancellation and statutory quality/defect routes. Narrow hygiene and clearance exclusions to the voluntary path and preserve statutory assessment.","Avoids treating house policy as the complete statement of customer rights or applying blanket exclusions.","Draft | Owner: Enterprise Retail Operations Manager | Pending approval; operational guidance, not legal advice."]},{"r":"11","cells":["08 Sep 2025\n0.9 / Procedure B","Define frontline intake, site-manager routine approval boundary and central exception authority; record customer communication, stock disposition and closure.","Allows routine service while reserving legally sensitive, disputed, ambiguous and exceptional cases for central review.","Draft | Owner: Enterprise Retail Operations Manager | Pending Nadia Sepulveda approval."]},{"r":"12","cells":["08 Sep 2025\n0.9 / Procedure C","During 15 September-31 October accept valid till-slip and portal evidence, assign/cross-reference one Return Case ID and reconcile daily. From 1 November make portal authoritative; retain a controlled outage queue.","Prevents duplicate refunds during dual running and preserves traceability when portal access is unavailable.","Draft | Owner: Enterprise Retail Operations Manager | Pending Nadia Sepulveda approval."]},{"r":"13","cells":["08 Sep 2025\n0.9 / Comparison A-B","Remove each exact duplicate once. Retain unambiguously linked malformed IDs; display unresolved malformed IDs separately and exclude only those from confirmed totals.","Provided groups do not overlap. This maintains a traceable confirmed population without treating unresolved records as proven invalid.","Draft | Owner: Enterprise Retail Operations Manager | Pending approval; inputs and formulas remain editable."]},{"r":"14","cells":["08 Sep 2025\n0.9 / Comparison C","Document confirmed growth alongside deterioration in duplicate incidence and the higher adjustment burden.","Raw value movement is GBP16,660; confirmed movement is GBP13,110; GBP3,550 is the increased exclusion burden.","Draft | Owner: Enterprise Retail Operations Manager | Pending Nadia Sepulveda approval."]},{"r":"15","cells":["08 Sep 2025\n0.9 / Document control","Set owner, approver, draft status, intended transition dates and future end-state date.","Makes the procedure approval-ready without claiming authorization before an approver decision.","Draft | Owner: Enterprise Retail Operations Manager | Approval authority: Nadia Sepulveda; decision pending."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required workbook exists at the top level of the submission under the exact filename `wexmoor_returns_decision_and_procedure.xlsx`.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file path and filename.","grader_hint":"Inspect the submission root; do not award this item for a renamed file, a file in a subdirectory, or a different format."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook opens without repair warnings, remains editable, and does not depend on macros, external links, or external data connections to display or recalculate its content.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Workbook open and recalculation behavior.","grader_hint":"Open the workbook in a standard spreadsheet application, recalculate it, and inspect for broken links, protected static-image substitutes, macros, and external connection prompts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Clearly identifiable sections labelled Decision, Operating Procedure, Comparison, and Change Log are present.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Visible workbook labels or named regions.","grader_hint":"Accept the labels as worksheet names or prominent section titles; all four must be readily locatable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Decision section is configured and readable as no more than one printed page.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Print area, page breaks, and rendered Decision section.","grader_hint":"Render or print-preview the Decision section using the workbook's configured settings. It must fit on one page without illegibly small text or clipped content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Operating Procedure section is configured and readable as no more than two printed pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Print area, page breaks, and rendered Operating Procedure section.","grader_hint":"Render or print-preview the procedure using the configured settings. It must fit within two pages without hidden, clipped, or unreadably scaled instructions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook identifies England and Wales as the jurisdiction and 8 September 2025 as the legal and policy as-of date.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Jurisdiction and as-of statement.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit jurisdiction and date in the decision or procedure, not merely a file creation date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure has usable document control showing an owner, approver, version or issue identifier, approval status, and intended effective or transition dates without falsely presenting the draft as already approved.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Document-control fields and status wording.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the workbook is approval-ready, that approval authority is identifiable, and that draft or pending status is not confused with authorization."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook states a practical purpose, scope, and audience covering the retail-site pilot and future enterprise baseline, while treating the legal content as operational guidance rather than legal advice.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Purpose, scope, audience, and boundary statements.","grader_hint":"A staff member and reviewer should be able to tell who uses the procedure, where it applies, and what the document does not purport to be."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The Decision section makes exactly one explicit recommendation rather than leaving multiple alternatives equally open.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Recommendation statement.","grader_hint":"Identify the operative recommendation. Conditional implementation is acceptable, but the approval choice itself must be singular and unambiguous."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The current cashier-led procedure and proposed portal-only central-approval procedure are compared on control consistency, customer handling, auditability, capacity, and transition feasibility.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Options comparison and supporting narrative.","grader_hint":"Award only if the comparison addresses both benefits and drawbacks material to the decision; a one-sided description of the preferred option is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The decision analysis identifies the central-review shortfall as forecast peak demand of 60 requests per day minus capacity of 35, equalling 25 requests per day with a tolerance of ±0 requests.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Capacity figures, formula, or stated shortfall.","grader_hint":"Verify that all three figures agree and that the analysis recognizes the absence of temporary-cover budget."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommendation adopts the stronger portal/control framework but does not require infeasible immediate portal-only central approval; it uses bounded delegation or triage during implementation rather than retaining the current process unchanged.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Recommended operating model and rationale.","grader_hint":"The defensible verdict is a controlled adoption of the proposed framework with a capacity-aware transition. Do not award if the workbook recommends an unchanged current process or ignores the 25-request daily shortfall."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The resource fallback is operationally bounded by defined case types, authority limits, logging, and escalation, rather than allowing unrestricted cashier discretion.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Fallback controls in the decision and procedure.","grader_hint":"Look for a workable division between routine policy cases and legally sensitive, disputed, or ambiguous cases, plus a record and escalation route."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommendation distinguishes the 15 September–31 October transition arrangement from the post-transition end state and gives each a coherent operating model.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Transition and end-state descriptions.","grader_hint":"Both periods must be explicit. A single process that assumes either immediate full deployment or permanent dual running does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every quantitative figure used to justify the recommendation agrees with the corresponding Comparison figure within ±£1 for monetary amounts, ±1 transaction for counts, and ±0.1 percentage point for percentages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Figures repeated across the Decision and Comparison sections.","grader_hint":"Cross-check repeated capacity, transaction, value, and movement figures inside the workbook. Do not award if conflicting versions of a key number appear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The Decision section closes with a clear approval call and does not end by deferring the decision to an unresolved options list or generic next-steps discussion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Closing portion of the Decision section.","grader_hint":"The final decision language should tell Nadia what is being recommended for approval."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The 1 March–31 May 2024 raw comparison population is shown as 1,240 lines with a value of £74,880, tolerances ±0 lines and ±£1.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"2024 raw count and value in the Comparison section.","grader_hint":"Check the displayed values and any underlying formulas."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The 1 March–31 May 2025 raw comparison population is shown as 1,390 lines with a value of £91,540, tolerances ±0 lines and ±£1.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"2025 raw count and value in the Comparison section.","grader_hint":"Check the displayed values and any underlying formulas."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Exact duplicate adjustments are shown as 28 lines and £1,680 for 2024 and 71 lines and £4,870 for 2025, each with tolerances ±0 lines and ±£1.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Duplicate adjustment rows or calculations.","grader_hint":"Verify both periods and ensure the entries are identified as exact duplicates rather than malformed-ID cases."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The malformed-ID populations reconcile in each period: 2024 has 14 lines/£910 split into nine/£590 linked and five/£320 unresolved; 2025 has 23/£1,740 split into 15/£1,060 linked and eight/£680 unresolved, with tolerances ±0 lines and ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Malformed-ID reconciliation.","grader_hint":"Confirm that linked plus unresolved equals the malformed total for both counts and values in each period."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The comparison method removes each exact duplicate once and records that duplicate and malformed-ID groups are non-overlapping.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Method note, formulas, and adjustment structure.","grader_hint":"Inspect whether duplicate lines are subtracted once only and whether the non-overlap assumption is documented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Malformed-ID lines that can be linked unambiguously remain in the confirmed population and are not deducted merely because their original ID was malformed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Confirmed-population formulas and treatment note.","grader_hint":"Verify that only unresolved malformed lines, not all malformed lines, are excluded from the confirmed figures."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Unresolved malformed-ID lines are kept visible as a separate unresolved population and excluded from confirmed figures without being described as proven invalid transactions.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Unresolved rows, labels, and limitation note.","grader_hint":"The treatment should preserve uncertainty: unresolved is not synonymous with duplicate, fraudulent, or invalid."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Confirmed line counts equal raw lines minus exact duplicates minus unresolved malformed lines: 1,207 for 2024 and 1,311 for 2025, tolerances ±0 lines.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Confirmed-count formulas and results.","grader_hint":"Check 1,240−28−5 and 1,390−71−8. Linked malformed lines must remain included."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Confirmed values equal raw value minus duplicate value minus unresolved value: £72,880 for 2024 and £85,990 for 2025, tolerances ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Confirmed-value formulas and results.","grader_hint":"Check £74,880−£1,680−£320 and £91,540−£4,870−£680."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Confirmed line movement is calculated as 1,311 minus 1,207, equalling an increase of 104 lines and 8.6%, with tolerances ±0 lines and ±0.1 percentage point.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Count movement calculation.","grader_hint":"Verify that the percentage uses the confirmed 2024 count as denominator."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Confirmed value movement is calculated as £85,990 minus £72,880, equalling an increase of £13,110 and 18.0%, with tolerances ±£1 and ±0.1 percentage point.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Value movement calculation.","grader_hint":"Verify that the percentage uses the confirmed 2024 value as denominator."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook quantifies deterioration in duplicate incidence: duplicate lines are approximately 2.3% of raw lines in 2024 and 5.1% in 2025, an increase of approximately 2.9 percentage points, each within ±0.1 percentage point.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Duplicate-rate calculation or material-change analysis.","grader_hint":"Check 28/1,240 and 71/1,390 and their percentage-point difference."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The material-change explanation distinguishes genuine confirmed growth from worsening data quality, noting that raw value rose by £16,660 while confirmed value rose by £13,110 and that the £3,550 difference reflects the larger period-on-period adjustment burden, each within ±£1.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Narrative and supporting movement calculations.","grader_hint":"The analysis must not attribute all apparent growth to dirty records or ignore the increased duplicate burden; it should explain both effects."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The comparison discloses that no line-level re-export was available, identifies the non-overlap and linkage assumptions, and avoids inventing transaction-level facts or unsupported precision.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Assumptions and limitations statement.","grader_hint":"Look for a candid limitation note and ensure the workbook does not fabricate dates, item types, customers, reasons, or approvals for the summarized lines."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The data-adjustment record makes the treatment of duplicates, linked malformed IDs, and unresolved IDs traceable to the resulting confirmed figures.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Adjustment table, formulas, notes, or linked change record.","grader_hint":"A reviewer should be able to follow each category from raw totals to confirmed totals without reverse-engineering unexplained hard-coded numbers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure clearly separates Wexmoor Press's voluntary 30-day change-of-mind policy from statutory consumer remedies and does not describe the house policy as the complete statement of customer rights.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Policy hierarchy and staff instructions.","grader_hint":"Look for an affirmative distinction that staff can apply, not only a generic statutory-rights disclaimer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure states that an in-store customer does not generally have a statutory right to return satisfactory goods merely for changing their mind, while preserving any applicable house-policy entitlement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"In-store change-of-mind rule.","grader_hint":"The wording should distinguish discretionary policy from remedies for faulty, misdescribed, or otherwise nonconforming goods."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"“Sale date” is replaced or pinned down operationally for immediate in-store supply, advance-paid click-and-collect, and delivered orders, using physical supply, collection, or delivery rather than a single ambiguous payment-date rule.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Definitions and eligibility-date instructions.","grader_hint":"Expect separate treatment for immediate possession, later collection, and delivery. The definition must be usable by staff and consistently applied."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure states a clear day-count convention for the house-policy window and labels it as an internal eligibility rule rather than asserting that the same clock governs every statutory remedy.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Timing definition and qualification.","grader_hint":"Accept a clear convention such as treating the supply, collection, or delivery date as day zero and counting from the following day, provided its internal-policy status is explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The ordinary change-of-mind path tests timeliness, proof of purchase, unopened or resaleable condition as applicable, product exclusions, and authority before approval.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Routine eligibility path.","grader_hint":"The procedure should translate the house rule into an executable check rather than merely repeat its wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Clearance status is treated as an exclusion from the voluntary change-of-mind policy, not as removal of statutory rights; any defect disclosed before sale is distinguished from a different or undisclosed defect.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Clearance-goods rule and exception handling.","grader_hint":"Look for both the voluntary exclusion and the statutory qualification. A general statement that all clearance sales are final is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The hygiene rule is confined to relevant sealed goods after the seal is broken and does not treat every personal-care item, opened package, or hygiene-labelled product as automatically ineligible under all return routes.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Hygiene-seal decision rule.","grader_hint":"The procedure should verify that a suitable seal existed and was broken, while routing defect or nonconformity claims separately."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Goods alleged to be faulty, not as described, unfit for purpose, or of unsatisfactory quality are routed to a statutory-remedy assessment regardless of clearance status, broken hygiene seal, opening, or expiry of the voluntary 30-day window.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Defect and nonconformity branch.","grader_hint":"The procedure need not promise a particular remedy in every case, but it must prevent staff from rejecting these claims solely under the change-of-mind exclusions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Any reference to the Consumer Rights Act short-term right to reject correctly relates it to nonconforming goods, distinguishes it from the house change-of-mind period, and avoids making “unopened” a condition of that statutory right.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Short-term rejection wording.","grader_hint":"Award if the legal rule is operationally accurate even without formal statutory citations; do not award if two different 30-day concepts are conflated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Distance-sale cancellation is treated as a separate route with the usual 14-day cancellation period measured from receipt of goods, and the procedure does not apply that cancellation right automatically to ordinary in-store sales.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Distance-cancellation branch and timing.","grader_hint":"Look for correct scope and timing as at the stated date. Minor plain-language phrasing is acceptable if it does not change the rule."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Click-and-collect cases are classified by where and how the contract was concluded rather than assuming that collection itself makes every transaction an in-store or distance sale.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Channel-classification instructions.","grader_hint":"The procedure should ask staff to distinguish an online completed purchase from an online reservation completed in store, escalating uncertainty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workflow keeps voluntary change-of-mind returns, distance cancellations, and quality or defect claims as separate decision paths with appropriately different eligibility questions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Decision tree, routing table, or equivalent procedure logic.","grader_hint":"A single undifferentiated 'within 30 days and unopened' test fails this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure asks for proof of purchase but permits credible alternatives to an original paper receipt and gives an escalation route when purchase evidence cannot be verified.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Evidence-of-purchase instructions.","grader_hint":"Examples may include an order record, payment record, or till lookup. The procedure should not promise approval where evidence remains inadequate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The operating sequence is executable from customer intake through classification, evidence and condition checks, authority decision, customer communication, refund or refusal handling, stock disposition, and record closure.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"End-to-end procedure flow.","grader_hint":"Walk a routine return and an exception through the procedure. Staff should not need to invent a missing handoff or closure action."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Roles and authority limits are explicit for frontline staff, the site manager or delegated approver, and central review during both transition and end state.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Responsibility or authority statements.","grader_hint":"The document must show who may approve routine cases, who records them, and which cases cannot be finalized locally."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The capacity-aware triage sends legally sensitive, disputed, ambiguous, or exceptional cases to central review while allowing defined routine cases to be resolved under controlled delegated authority.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Triage and escalation rules.","grader_hint":"Confirm that triage addresses the 35-versus-60 constraint without weakening the statutory safeguards or recreating unrestricted cashier discretion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"During 15 September–31 October, the procedure accepts both valid till-slip and portal evidence, assigns or cross-references a single return case identifier, and reconciles dual-system activity to prevent duplicate refunds.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Transition-period capture and reconciliation controls.","grader_hint":"Look for a concrete anti-duplication control and a regular reconciliation responsibility, not merely a statement that two systems are in use."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The end-state procedure identifies the portal as the authoritative returns register and includes a controlled outage or unavailable-system fallback requiring queued records to be captured and reconciled later.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"End-state and continuity instructions.","grader_hint":"The fallback must preserve traceability; silent till-only processing or an instruction simply to stop serving customers is not sufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The return record captures enough information for audit and reconciliation—original transaction reference, channel and date basis, reason or legal route, item and seal condition where relevant, decision, authority, value, outcome, and timestamps—without soliciting unnecessary sensitive personal data.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Required record fields and data-handling instruction.","grader_hint":"Assess whether the record supports later review of eligibility and duplicate prevention while remaining proportionate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure identifies material escalation cases, including unclear contract channel, disputed condition or disclosed defect, unresolved transaction identity, suspected duplicate refund, customer challenge involving statutory rights, and cases outside delegated authority.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Escalation criteria and destination.","grader_hint":"Equivalent clearly defined categories are acceptable. Each must lead to an identifiable reviewer or holding action rather than a dead end."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The Change Log records substantive changes and judgments, including the new sale-date definition, narrowed handling of hygiene and clearance exclusions, transition and authority controls, data-cleaning treatment, rationale, status, and approval trace.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Change Log entries.","grader_hint":"A blank template or a log containing only cosmetic edits does not satisfy this item; the main policy, process, and analytical judgments must be traceable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook is practical for staff and oversight use: navigation is obvious, formulas and inputs are distinguishable, legal qualifications sit beside the affected rules, procedure language is concise, and no essential instruction is hidden in notes or unreadable text.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered workbook and editable cell structure.","grader_hint":"Review the artifact as both a store operator and a compliance reviewer. Technically correct content that cannot be found or followed should not receive this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Penalty: the workbook states or operationally implements a blanket rule that hygiene-sealed or clearance goods can never be returned under any circumstances, thereby purporting to extinguish statutory rights solely because of those labels.","weight":-8.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Any categorical exclusion in the decision, procedure, comparison commentary, or customer-facing wording.","grader_hint":"Apply the penalty when an affirmative blanket exclusion appears, even if a generic statutory-rights disclaimer appears elsewhere. Do not apply merely because the workbook accurately excludes these goods from the voluntary change-of-mind path."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Vellumstone Associates is advising Wexmoor Press on a returns control that must function through a staged system migration and withstand compliance review. The recommendation must balance legal accuracy, data quality, customer operations, and a central-review capacity shortfall.","difficulty_sources":["Separating confirmed period movement from worsening duplicate and malformed-record incidence","Translating a voluntary returns policy into operational rules without misstating statutory consumer rights","Resolving the ambiguous meaning of sale date across payment, collection, and delivery","Designing a controlled fallback for a 25-request-per-day central-review capacity gap","Supporting simultaneous legacy and portal evidence during migration while defining a distinct end state","Keeping the decision and procedure concise enough to meet strict print-page limits"],"authoring_plan":{"solver_instance":"The solver receives no reference files and must create a single editable workbook from the facts in the request and professional knowledge of retail returns operations and England-and-Wales consumer rules as at the stated date.","imperfections_to_preserve":["The two period summaries contain exact duplicates and malformed transaction identifiers, but linked malformed records can be retained while unresolved records cannot be treated as confirmed.","The source groups are expressly non-overlapping, preventing a defensible solution from subtracting the same lines twice.","The phrase “sale date” is operationally ambiguous across immediate in-store supply, advance-paid collection, and delivery.","The house policy's hygiene and clearance language is easy to overextend into an unlawful blanket refusal of statutory remedies.","Peak demand exceeds the sole central reviewer's capacity, and no temporary resource can be added.","The portal and legacy till evidence coexist during a defined transition before the portal becomes the end-state register."],"numeric_gold_rules":{"confirmed_population":"For each period, confirmed count equals raw lines minus exact duplicate lines minus unresolved malformed-ID lines. Confirmed value equals raw value minus exact duplicate value minus unresolved malformed-ID value. Unambiguously linked malformed-ID records remain included.","confirmed_results_for_validation":{"2024_confirmed_lines":1207,"2024_confirmed_value_gbp":72880,"2025_confirmed_lines":1311,"2025_confirmed_value_gbp":85990},"movement":"Absolute movement equals 2025 confirmed less 2024 confirmed. Percentage movement uses the 2024 confirmed figure as denominator.","movement_results_for_validation":{"confirmed_line_change":104,"confirmed_line_change_percent":8.6164,"confirmed_value_change_gbp":13110,"confirmed_value_change_percent":17.9885},"data_quality":"Duplicate-line rate equals exact duplicate lines divided by raw lines. The rates are approximately 2.2581% and 5.1079%, a deterioration of approximately 2.8498 percentage points.","raw_vs_confirmed":"Raw value movement is £16,660. Confirmed value movement is £13,110. The £3,550 difference equals the increase in total exclusions between periods: £5,550 in 2025 less £2,000 in 2024."},"intended_decision":{"verdict":"Recommend adoption of the proposed portal and control framework, but reject immediate portal-only central approval as infeasible. Use a bounded, logged delegation and triage model during transition, with central review reserved for legally sensitive, disputed, ambiguous, or exceptional cases.","transition_behavior":"Both valid till-slip and portal records can evidence a return during the migration window, but each case must have one return identifier or cross-reference and be reconciled to prevent duplicate refunds.","end_state_behavior":"The portal becomes the authoritative register after transition. Routine approvals may remain controlled and delegated where needed, while exception classes retain central escalation. A logged outage queue must later be entered and reconciled."},"doctrinal_rules_and_prohibited_claims":[{"rule":"The 30-day unopened rule is a voluntary change-of-mind policy.","must_not_claim":"It is the complete measure of statutory rights or a statutory unopened-goods requirement."},{"rule":"There is generally no statutory right to return satisfactory in-store purchases solely because the consumer changed their mind.","must_not_claim":"Every in-store customer has a general statutory 30-day change-of-mind right."},{"rule":"Clearance goods may be excluded from the voluntary change-of-mind policy, while statutory rights survive except in relation to a specific defect disclosed before purchase.","must_not_claim":"Clearance goods are final sale under all circumstances."},{"rule":"The hygiene exception is narrow and depends on a suitable seal having been broken; defect and nonconformity claims follow a separate route.","must_not_claim":"Every hygiene-labelled, opened, or personal-care item is unreturnable."},{"rule":"Faulty, misdescribed, unfit, or unsatisfactory goods must be considered under statutory remedy rules even when opened, reduced, hygiene-related, or outside the voluntary policy window.","must_not_claim":"Opening, clearance status, a broken hygiene seal, or the house-policy deadline automatically extinguishes those rights."},{"rule":"Distance-sale cancellation is a distinct route with the usual 14-day period measured from receipt of goods.","must_not_claim":"The distance cancellation right applies automatically to ordinary in-store purchases."},{"rule":"Click-and-collect classification depends on where and how the contract was concluded.","must_not_claim":"Collection alone conclusively makes the transaction an in-store sale or a distance sale."},{"rule":"Proof of purchase may be established by credible evidence other than an original paper receipt.","must_not_claim":"An original paper receipt is invariably a statutory prerequisite."}],"operational_expectations":["Define a consistent internal eligibility date for immediate supply, later collection, and delivery, with a clear counting convention.","Separate voluntary change-of-mind, distance-cancellation, and nonconforming-goods paths before applying condition or product exclusions.","Assign intake, routine approval, exception review, recording, reconciliation, and final authorization responsibilities.","Use capacity-aware triage without giving frontline staff unrestricted discretion.","Capture enough information to support eligibility review, duplicate prevention, audit, and later reconciliation while minimizing personal data.","Include customer communication, stock disposition, refund or refusal handling, escalation, and case closure.","Maintain an end-state outage fallback that preserves a queued audit trail and requires later portal capture."],"required_local_vocabulary":{"section_labels":["Decision","Operating Procedure","Comparison","Change Log"],"source":"All four labels and the exact output filename are stated in the request."},"change_record_expectations":"The record should capture the sale-date interpretation, legal and policy boundary clarifications, transition controls, authority design, reconciliation treatment, rationale, version or date, approval status, and affected content. It must record substantive judgments rather than merely formatting edits.","offline_feasibility_check":"An imagined reference workbook was derived using standard spreadsheet formulas, rendered through an offline office suite, and walked against all rubric items. All quantitative predicates derive from the request, all doctrinal items are reachable from occupational knowledge, and no item requires internet access or an unavailable source."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"returns_decision_procedure","filename":"wexmoor_returns_decision_and_procedure.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"Editable decision workbook containing the recommendation, returns operating procedure, comparison analysis, and change record.","required":true,"constraints":["Place the file at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename.","Include clearly labelled Decision, Operating Procedure, Comparison, and Change Log sections.","Keep the Decision section to one printed page and the Operating Procedure section to no more than two printed pages.","Keep formulas, assumptions, and change records editable and inspectable.","Do not use macros, external data connections, or links that are required to read or recalculate the workbook."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"make_decisions","work_product":"operating_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"general_operations_managers","sector":"retail_trade","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":8.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"The reference solution should be reviewed independently by one England-and-Wales retail consumer-law or compliance specialist and one spreadsheet and retail-operations reviewer. Numeric formulas, print limits, transition controls, and every affirmative legal proposition must be checked before acceptance.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No line-level transaction records are available, so the grader can validate reconciliation logic and disclosed assumptions but cannot verify individual duplicate or malformed transactions.","The workbook is an operational control document rather than a substitute for matter-specific legal advice.","The summarized data does not support analysis by product, customer, return reason, approval outcome, or store channel."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:00:21+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:00:21+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:00:21+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:00:21+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/63860b400c19c9e9","declared_deliverables":["wexmoor_returns_decision_and_procedure.xlsx"]};
